title: 'collator-protocol: check v3 candidate against last finished slot block'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    # Description

    This PR achieves the following:
    1) removes the assumption that the scheduling parent sent with a candidate descriptor is an active leaf on the collator-side
    2) removes the reputation penalty for collators sending a candidate with a scheduling parent that's corresponding to an in progress slot
    3) checks on the validator_side that the candidate descriptor's scheduling parent is the rc block corresponding to the last finished rc slot's block.

    ## Integration

    N/A

    ## Review Notes

    Fixes #11169

    Cumulus side here: https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/pull/11241
    Tests were done against the cumulus PR + the corresponding scheduling parent picking logic when building block (async backing with v2/v3 collations). Additional tests were made for the case of elastic scaling too (v2 & v3 alike). As a bonus, the changed logic removes the `slot_offset` for V3 collations building.
